n annotation processor, and the deciding factor is whether *test source* defines new Micronaut-annotated types needing compile-time processing (as with sourcegen's code-generating annotations). Since `@Secured`/`@RunAs`/`@CreatedBy`/`@UpdatedBy` are plain reflectable markers with no code-generation or bean-processing requirement, a test can exercise them via ordinary reflection without `micronaut-inject-java`. This validates the earlier decision — no changes needed.\n\n**Final decision (unchanged):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"no_action\",\n  \"summary\": \"micronaut-security-annotations:5.3.2 is a small marker-annotation jar (RUNTIME retention, no code-gen, no bound interceptor); its only compile deps (micronaut-inject/micronaut-aop) resolve transitively via the artifact itself, so the generated scaffold's testImplementation on the coordinate is sufficient. No Docker image, extra dependency, or env/system property is needed.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Test these annotations (@Secured, @RunAs, @CreatedBy, @UpdatedBy) via plain reflection on annotated classes/methods/fields (retention, target, declared values) — enforcement/interception logic lives in the separate io.micronaut.security:micronaut-security core artifact, not in this jar, so don't assume AOP interception or a running security filter is exercisable here. No testAnnotationProcessor is needed since these annotations are plain markers, not code-generating (unlike micronaut-sourcegen-annotations).\",\n  \"risks\": [\"The internal SecuredEvaluationContextRegistrar SPI class only participates in Micronaut's compile-time expression-evaluation processing when a consumer uses expression-style @Secured values; ordinary role-string usage won't exercise it, so it may end up with little or no direct coverage — that's expected given this artifact's scope.\"]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":7529,"type":"result","duration_ms":7540,"uuid":"35dead16-2ddd-4c2f-ab05-d883df528156","ttft_stream_ms":138